---
description: Git and safety workflow for the Ledgerly revamp
alwaysApply: true
---
- Work only on the "revamp" branch. Never push commits to main. main changes only through a pull request created with gh pr create and merged with gh pr merge --merge, only when I explicitly ask for a release; never --squash, --rebase or --delete-branch (the revamp branch stays). After a merge: git switch revamp; git pull --ff-only origin main; push tags only.
- One phase = one commit (or a small series) with message "phase <ID>: <summary>". Before committing run lint, the TypeScript check (once TS is set up) and "next build". If anything fails, fix it or report it; do not commit a broken build silently.
- After each phase commit, create the tag "phase-<ID>" and push the branch and tags if a remote exists.
- Never run git push --force, git reset --hard, git clean -fd, or rewrite history unless I explicitly ask.
- Stay inside the scope of the current phase. At the end, list every file you changed.
- Never print or commit secrets (.env values, API keys, connection strings, passwords).
- Destructive database operations (migrate reset, truncate, deleteMany over tables, a seed that wipes data) need my explicit confirmation in chat and a fresh backup first. Print the target database host (never credentials) before running them.
- Database migrations must be additive only (new indexes, new nullable columns) while main is deployed. Never edit an already-applied migration. No drops or renames.
- At the end of every phase report: summary, files changed, how I can verify it manually, and known issues.

## Testing (lean)
- Default check before a commit: "npm run check" (lint + typecheck + build). That is enough for UI-only phases; write no new tests for them.
- Run Vitest only if you changed code covered by tests/. Add unit tests only when a phase changes logic.
- Run "npm run test:e2e:quick" (Maya only: dashboard and her default account page, fail on page errors or 5xx) only when a phase changes data fetching, auth or routing. Never run the full six-user suite or the perf baseline unless I ask.
- Tests may write to the database only for demo users and must restore what they change. Never delete or skip a test to get green.
- Put something under NEEDS HUMAN only if it truly cannot be automated.
